# Architecture & timeline log

Living doc: `rummy-home3/docs/architecture-and-timeline.md`

## When to update it

Update that file in the same change set when any of these happen:

- New or replaced tool (EAS, Expo SDK bump, Supabase, GitHub Pages, CI, store accounts)
- Distribution path changes (Expo Go vs EAS Build vs Play/TestFlight)
- Major module finished or abandoned (auth, scoring, players, store submit)
- Account/linking status that blockers care about (EAS login, projectId, env vars pushed)

## How to write entries

- Prefer **Timeline** bullets: date + one or two sentences on *what tool/architecture changed and why*
- Update **Current stack** and **Module status** tables when they drift
- Do **not** dump code diffs, file lists, or minor UI polish
- Keep the “big picture” Expo ≠ leaving Expo section accurate if distribution story changes

## When not to update

Pure copy tweaks, small bugfixes, styling-only passes with no new dependency or hosting change.
